ls about domestic  violence maybe in the moment when they  are experiencing those things  things will click a little bit a little  bit quicker that kind of proactive  action is exactly what the shade tree is  trying to take the domestic violence  shelter provides housing and case  management for survivors  but now they're working on direct  outreach at local casinos businesses and  organizations  to get ahead of the issue whether we put  a booth up or you ask us to come speak  because awareness for us is very  important and it's key to bringing the  issue to life  they hope to start by this october and  survivors say that's a great idea  if someone would have came to talk to us  just all as a group saying like  you can come here you can have someone  to talk to it would have been  such a relief courtney is in a much  better place now but her healing  continues  i feel like i'm getting myself back but  i'm not totally  there yet now metro police tell us that  they are also working with organizations  to try to stop this issue before these  domestic situations  escalate to those in need there are some  resources for you can call  the national domestic violence hotline  at 1-800-799-7233  and the shade tree also has a 24 7  crisis line  at 1-855-385-0072  reporting live tonight orco mana 8 news  now

